# AWS → Cloudflare Migration Preference (CUSTOMIZED FOR cloudless.gr)

## Direction
- **Target platform:** Cloudflare Workers, R2, D1, Access, Tunnel, DNS/CDN.
- **Primary goal:** Migrate *all* existing AWS resources (SSM, SES, S3, Lambda, Athena, etc.) to their Cloudflare equivalents **or** retire them.
- **Exception policy:** Keep an AWS resource **only** if a clear migration path does **not** exist *and* the user explicitly requests it.

## Tooling – Hard rule (adjusted for this repo)

- **Never install the AWS CLI** (`aws`, `awscli`, or any `aws*` binary) on a developer machine, CI runner, or production host **unless** you are actively migrating a legacy AWS resource and have documented the migration plan.
- **Never add a new AWS SDK** (`@aws-sdk/*`, `boto3`, etc.) to the codebase.  
  - If you need to read an existing AWS resource, use the **existing in‑repo wrapper** (e.g., `src/lib/aws-compat.ts`) and **immediately replace it** with a Cloudflare‑native call (R2 SDK, D1 client, etc.).
- **Allowed Cloudflare tooling:** `wrangler`, `node-fetch`, `axios`, `@cloudflare/workers-types`, `miniflare`, `tunnel-cli`.

## Cloudflare‑specific references (added for this project)

| AWS Service | Cloudflare Equivalent | Example Resource in this repo |
|------------|----------------------|------------------------------|
| S3 (object storage) | **R2** bucket | `cloudless-assets`, `cloudless-analytics`, `app-media-bucket`, `datalake-bucket` |
| DynamoDB / Aurora | **D1** database | `user-auth-db` |
| SNS / SES | **Email Workers** (or external ESP) | `email-sender.ts` |
| Lambda | **Workers** | All API routes under `src/app/api/*` |
| CloudFront | **Cloudflare CDN** (automatic) | All static assets served via `*.cloudflare.com` |
| IAM / Secrets Manager | **Wrangler Secrets** | `wrangler secret put` commands in CI |

> **Tip:** When you see a reference to an AWS ARN, think “map it to a Cloudflare Worker route + R2 bucket / D1 table”.

## Prohibited actions (reinforced)

- ❌ `apt-get install awscli` / `pip install awscli`  
- ❌ `npm i @aws-sdk/client-s3` (unless removing an existing AWS call)  
- ❌ Any `aws` command in CI scripts – replace with `wrangler` or `cf` equivalents.

